# ─── Novelty Experiment results are EVIDENCE, not scratch ────────────
# The blanket `results/` rule above was hiding every N1-N11 result JSON: the numbers
# quoted in NOVELTY_STATUS.md and the paper existed only on one laptop. Track them.
# Large regenerable inputs (M2_features.npy, embeddings/) stay ignored.
!Novelty Experiment/results/
!Novelty Experiment/results/**

# M28 writes its outputs twice - once at the top of Barshon's/M28/ (tracked) and once
# into results_M28/ plus a zip bundle. The duplicates are regenerable; keep one copy.
Barshon's/M28/results_M28/
Barshon's/M28/M28_master_results_bundle.zip

# ─── Model `Results/` directories are EVIDENCE too ───────────────────
# Found 2026-08-30: `core.ignorecase = true` on Windows makes the blanket `results/`
# rule above match `Results/` as well, so it was hiding three directories that hold the
# numbers behind most of the paper's tables:
#     Asif's/M22_v2/Results          the best model (0.5602) and its verbatim-official
#                                    companion run (0.5641)
#     Asif's/M3_v2/Results           the no-augmentation control, ablation row A1
#     M40_M43_transformers/Results   all six ViT / Swin-T / DeiT-S runs
# This is the same fault as the Novelty Experiment one above, from the same rule, found
# the same way. Track the evidence; keep the regenerable weights and arrays ignored.
!**/Results/
!**/Results/**
**/Results/*.pth
**/Results/*.npy
**/Results/cache/

# ─── M48 core-pipeline ablation ──────────────────────────────────────
# Same trap as the two above: the blanket `*.npy` rule would have hidden the per-cycle
# prediction dumps, which are the INPUT to every paired test in Tier A — a few tens of KB
# each, and not regenerable without the GPU run that produced them. Track those; keep the
# spectrogram cache (regenerable, ~1 GB) and the checkpoints ignored.
!M48_core_pipeline_ablation/preds_M48_*.npy
M48_core_pipeline_ablation/cache/
M48_core_pipeline_ablation/*.pth
